@@ -5,9 +5,18 @@ Changelog
 Upcoming version (not yet released)
 -----------------------------------
 
+Added
+^^^^^
+
+- Added physical pen-tip/whiteboard collision sensing and a bounded contact-force
+  penalty to the G1 drawing task.
+
 Changed
 ^^^^^^^
 
+- Changed the G1 whiteboard task to hold a reachable center target before following
+  a continuous Gerono figure eight, with matching timing in training and playback.
+- Extended the drawing episode so it includes a complete figure-eight cycle.
 - Bumped ``rsl-rl-lib`` from 5.4.2 to 5.5.0. This update removes the ``logger_type``
   attribute of the ``rsl_rl.utils.Logger``, so code that previously checked
   ``logger.logger_type`` must instead check the type of ``logger.writer``.
@@ -15,6 +24,16 @@ Changed
 Fixed
 ^^^^^
 
+- Restored the shared Unitree G1 asset (``g1.xml``) to its pristine, task-agnostic
+  form. A prior commit had hardcoded a pen, a whiteboard, and a partial
+  ``<actuator>`` block (waist and arms only) directly into the robot XML, which
+  left every leg joint unactuated in floating-base environments and caused the
+  robot to appear frozen or collapsed during training and playback. The pen and
+  whiteboard are now added purely programmatically by the drawing task, and all
+  29 joints are actuated through ``G1_ARTICULATION`` as intended.
+- Removed the dead legacy ``whiteboard/env_cfg.py`` and ``whiteboard/mdp/commands.py``
+  modules (an unused, superseded circle-drawing command path) that were not
+  registered or imported anywhere.
 - Capped ``wandb`` below 0.29, which removed the ``start_method`` setting still passed
   by ``rsl-rl-lib`` and crashed training runs launched with ``--logger wandb``.
 - ``distribution="gaussian"`` domain randomization now draws an independent value per
